{
  "title": "Dunder Mifflin Idol",
  "logline": "Michael stages a talent show to win Jan's approval and gets a room fight with Angela's potluck, a blank sign-up sheet, and a sincere moment he can't hide, while Pam gets overlooked by Roy and Jim finally notices.",
  "outline": "A: Michael books the conference room for \"Dunder Mifflin Idol\" to impress Jan; Angela's Fall Harvest Potluck has it first; sign-ups stall, Toby stays with him. B: Jim and Pam prank Dwight (Jell-O stapler); Roy stands Pam up and barely notices her; Jim drives her home. C: Creed and Kevin's band Scrantonicity; Angela and Dwight's beet secret leaks. Order: cold, A, B, A, C, A, B, C, A, B, A, tag.",
  "theme": "Wanting to be seen, and noticing who already sees you.",
  "storySoFar": "Michael is desperate for Jan's approval and has announced Dunder Mifflin Idol for Friday at four in the conference room, a room Angela's Party Planning Committee had booked for its Fall Harvest Potluck. Dwight, promoted to emcee with a laminated badge, is chasing status. Jim keeps pranking Dwight with Pam, the latest prank being a stapler in lime Jell-O. Pam is still engaged to Roy, who keeps postponing the wedding and barely notices her; Jim noticed her earrings. Creed, Kevin and Creed's shakers are in Scrantonicity. Angela and Dwight have a secret the office half-knows. Michael has a standing feud with Toby, who keeps being told he is not invited.",
  "extras": [],
